1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,760
To master a craft, the first step is to find someone already skilled, a true mentor who lights

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:11,120
the path ahead. Great teachers are like lanterns in the fog, helping you see what you might miss

3
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:17,040
on your own. Seeking knowledge is like planting a precious seed in your heart. With daily diligence,

4
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:22,960
patience and care, it will grow roots. Each lesson, no matter how small, adds nourishment,

5
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:28,960
water it with curiosity, and guard it with perseverance. Sooner or later, it will sprout.

6
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:34,720
Keep learning the good, the right, and the harmonious. And you will succeed, not just in skill,

7
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:41,120
but in character. Mastery is not built in a day, but in many quiet mornings and determined evenings.

8
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:47,280
You must also learn to train yourself. If you're unsure, follow the footsteps of those before you.

9
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:53,200
The path will appear where once there was only doubt. Trust the journey. Even stumbles become

10
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:58,960
part of your foundation. Don't grow up in the dark alone. Learn skillfully, work diligently.

11
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:04,640
Even the hardest stone can be shaped into gold by a steady hand. Don't be afraid to fail.

12
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:10,160
Be afraid of standing still. With time and persistence, you'll surely succeed. Steady hands,

13
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:16,400
steady heart, steady craft. Let each day be a step forward, no matter how small. In the end,

14
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:18,880
you will look back and see just how far you've come.

